The last results look corrupted: different entities share one LEI, and E10 shows E04's LEI. I won't use them. I'll re-run with simpler queries that avoid the LEI join.

```sparql
PREFIX lad: <https://example.org/ladder/>
SELECT ?t ?b ?d ?act ?r WHERE {
 ?a lad:ratedThing ?t; lad:ratingType lad:type-LTIDR; lad:date ?d; lad:action ?act; lad:rating ?r.
 OPTIONAL{?a lad:ccyBasis ?b}
 FILTER(?r IN ("RD","D") || (?act=lad:action-DG && ?d>="2026-01-01"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date>))
} ORDER BY ?t ?d
```

```sparql
PREFIX lad: <https://example.org/ladder/>
SELECT ?t ?type ?c ?s ?p WHERE {
 { ?t lad:parent ?p } UNION { ?t lad:entityType lad:etype-SOV }
 OPTIONAL{?t lad:entityType ?type} OPTIONAL{?t lad:country ?c} OPTIONAL{?t lad:sourceSystem ?s}
} ORDER BY ?t
```

```sparql
PREFIX lad: <https://example.org/ladder/>
